Origin: or עֲרֻגָה; feminine passive participle of 6165;
Meaning: something piled up (as if (figuratively) raised by mental aspiration), i.e. a paterre
KJV renders: bed, furrow.

H6171.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 6166;
Meaning: an onager (from his lonesome habits)
KJV renders: wild ass.

H6172.strongs:
Origin: from 6168;
Meaning: nudity, literally (especially the pudenda) or figuratively (disgrace, blemish)
KJV renders: nakedness, shame, unclean(-ness).

H6173.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 6172;
Meaning: nakedness, i.e. (figuratively) impoverishment
KJV renders: dishonor.

H6174.strongs:
Origin: or עָרֹם; from 6191 (in its original sense);
Meaning: nude, either partially or totally
KJV renders: naked.

H6175.strongs:
Origin: passive participle of 6191;
Meaning: cunning (usually in a bad sense)
KJV renders: crafty, prudent, subtil.

H6176.strongs:
Origin: or עַרְעָר; from 6209 reduplicated;
Meaning: a juniper (from its nudity of situation)
KJV renders: health.

H6177.strongs:
Origin: or עֲרֹעֵר; or עַרְעוֹר; the same as 6176; nudity of situation;
Meaning: Aroër, the name of three places in or near Palestine
KJV renders: Aroer.

H6178.strongs:
Origin: passive participle of 6206;
Meaning: feared, i.e. (concretely) a horrible place or chasm
KJV renders: cliffs.

H6179.strongs:
Origin: from 5782; watchful;
Meaning: Eri, an Israelite
KJV renders: Eri.

H6180.strongs:
Origin: patronymically of 6179;
Meaning: an Erite (collectively) or descendants of Eri
KJV renders: Erites.

H6181.strongs:
Origin: for 6172;
Meaning: nudity
KJV renders: bare, naked, × quite.

H6182.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to comminute;
Meaning: meal
KJV renders: dough.

H6183.strongs:
Origin: from 6201;
Meaning: the sky (as drooping at the horizon)
KJV renders: heaven.

H6184.strongs:
Origin: from 6206;
Meaning: fearful, i.e. powerful or tyrannical
KJV renders: mighty, oppressor, in great power, strong, terrible, violent.

H6185.strongs:
Origin: from 6209;
Meaning: bare, i.e. destitute (of children)
KJV renders: childless.

H6186.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to set in a row, i.e. arrange, put in order (in a very wide variety of applications)
KJV renders: put (set) (the battle, self) in array, compare, direct, equal, esteem, estimate, expert (in war), furnish, handle, join (battle), ordain, (lay, put, reckon up, set) (in) order, prepare, tax, value.

H6187.strongs:
Origin: from 6186;
Meaning: a pile, equipment, estimate
KJV renders: equal, estimation, (things that are set in) order, price, proportion, × set at, suit, taxation, × valuest.

H6188.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root; properly, to strip; but used as denominative from 6189;
Meaning: to expose or remove the prepuce, whether literal (to go naked) or figurative (to refrain from using)
KJV renders: count uncircumcised, foreskin to be uncovered.

H6189.strongs:
Origin: from 6188;
Meaning: properly, exposed, i.e. projecting loose (as to the prepuce); used only technically, uncircumcised (i.e. still having the prepuce uncurtailed)
KJV renders: uncircumcised (person).

H6190.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 6189;
Meaning: the prepuce
KJV renders: foreskin, uncircumcised.

H6191.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to be (or make) bare; but used only in the derivative sense (through the idea perhaps of smoothness) to be cunning (usually in a bad sense)
KJV renders: × very, beware, take crafty (counsel), be prudent, deal subtilly.

H6192.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to pile up
KJV renders: gather together.

H6193.strongs:
Origin: from 6191;
Meaning: a stratagem
KJV renders: craftiness.

H6194.strongs:
Origin: (Jeremiah 50:26) or (feminine) עֲרֵמָה; from 6192;
Meaning: a heap; specifically, a sheaf
KJV renders: heap (of corn), sheaf.

H6195.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 6193;
Meaning: trickery; or (in a good sense) discretion
KJV renders: guile, prudence, subtilty, wilily, wisdom.

H6196.strongs:
Origin: probably from 6191;
Meaning: the plane tree (from its smooth and shed bark)
KJV renders: chestnut tree.

H6197.strongs:
Origin: probably from 5782; watchful;
Meaning: Eran, an Israelite
KJV renders: Eran.

H6198.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 6197;
Meaning: an Eranite or descendant (collectively) of Eran
KJV renders: Eranites.

H6199.strongs:
Origin: from 6209;
Meaning: naked, i.e. (figuratively) poor
